Given,

\begin{gathered}
A=10 \text { units } \\
B=20 \text { units } \\
\theta=30^{\circ}
\end{gathered}

 \\ $<img src="/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fcomedk%252Fa6uk2jhCRLPL90WG7sf0yPIyYb5Xpb3l28HhCzbB3D8.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2" data-qx-orig-src="https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fcomedk%2Fa6uk2jhCRLPL90WG7sf0yPIyYb5Xpb3l28HhCzbB3D8.original.fullsize.png?alt=media" data-qx-storage-src="https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fcomedk%2Fa6uk2jhCRLPL90WG7sf0yPIyYb5Xpb3l28HhCzbB3D8.original.fullsize.png?alt=media">$ \\ 
The given situation is shown in the figure. The angle between $\mathbf{A}$ and $\mathbf{B}$,

\theta=180^{\circ}-30^{\circ}-30^{\circ}=120^{\circ}

$\therefore$ Magnitude of the resultant vector,

\begin{aligned}
R &=\sqrt{A^{2}+B^{2}+2 A B \cos \theta} \\
&=\sqrt{10^{2}+20^{2}+2 \times 10 \times 20 \cos 120^{\circ}} \\
&=\sqrt{100+400-200} \\
&=10 \sqrt{3}
\end{aligned}

The given situation is shown below
<br><img src="/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fcomedk%252Fye0OOu5L-Sh-WZF9Ui9WXR72J0rC-pIT3yXCJTSPCDo.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2" data-qx-orig-src="https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fcomedk%2Fye0OOu5L-Sh-WZF9Ui9WXR72J0rC-pIT3yXCJTSPCDo.original.fullsize.png?alt=media" data-qx-storage-src="https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fcomedk%2Fye0OOu5L-Sh-WZF9Ui9WXR72J0rC-pIT3yXCJTSPCDo.original.fullsize.png?alt=media"><br>

\begin{aligned}
&v_{A}=10 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s} \\
&v_{B}=6 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s}
\end{aligned}

The two boys meet at point $C$ after a time $t$. Horizontal component of velocity of $v_{A}$.

\begin{aligned}
v_{A B} &=v_{A} \cos \theta=10 \cos \theta \\
&=10\left(\frac{\sqrt{10^{2}-6^{2}}}{10}\right) \\
&=8 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s} \\
\therefore \quad t &=\frac{A B}{v_{A B}}=\frac{200}{8}=25 \mathrm{~s}
\end{aligned}
